# Five Federation destroyers on layouts/group-move.jsonc are selected together and ordered to one point: each gets its own
# move order to a cell of the game's group formation around it. The fast-forward runs the world, undrawn, until every
# order has ended, and the dump then shows each at its cell with move=none. The dump while they drive shows each ship's own move=<x>,<z>.
# Run it with --layout layouts/group-move.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
# The point is in the frame of the dump's pos= field, whose z is the layout z mirrored.
wait 0.5
box A B C D E
wait 0.3
move 2000 -2200
wait 1
dump driving
fast-forward until A move = none max 60
fast-forward until B move = none max 60
fast-forward until C move = none max 60
fast-forward until D move = none max 60
fast-forward until E move = none max 60
dump arrived
